&lt;h2 id="garden-description">Garden Description&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>A fish-curing factory (&lt;em>salsamenta&lt;/em>) located to the SE of the Nymfarum domus was renovated between the IInd and the IIIrd centuries. Among the changes made was the design of a small house organized around a small peristyle garden (4 x 4 m.) (XXII) and bound by a low wall that curved to make a semi-circular basin (Plan view, Fig.1; ).&lt;/p>
&lt;p>During the second half of the IVth century, with the abandonment of the industrial unit, the residential area was enlarged and a second semi-circular basin was added in the garden.&lt;/p>
